# i3 config file (v4)
#
# The v4 marker is load-bearing — see the shared config for why.
#
# No per-side outer gap here: tauler-e2e reads i3's `gaps` field as an absolute
# and it is only absolute while the global default is zero (docs/adr/0015).
# `smart_borders` is an i3-gaps directive that native i3 4.22 rejects outright,
# which raises i3-nagbar over the top of the screenshot — see monolith/i3.config.

font pango:JetBrains Mono 10

gaps inner 10

default_border pixel 2
new_window pixel 2

# border, background, text, indicator, child border.
client.focused          #DFB22E #1A2038 #E9E7DC #DFB22E #DFB22E
client.unfocused        #2A3350 #1A2038 #7F8AA6 #2A3350 #2A3350
client.focused_inactive #2A3350 #1A2038 #7F8AA6 #2A3350 #2A3350
client.urgent           #B04A3A #1A2038 #E9E7DC #B04A3A #B04A3A
